                "senderName": "NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued October 21 at 11:02AM MST until October 21 at 3:00PM MST by NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "description": "FFWFGZ\n\nThe National Weather Service in Flagstaff has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nThe Moenkopi Wash in...\nCoconino County in north central Arizona...\n\n* Until 300 PM MST /400 PM MDT/.\n\n* At 1102 AM MST /1202 PM MDT/, a river gauge on the Moenkopi Wash\nreported a rapid rise of around 8 feet from thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain over the Moenkopi Wash. Flash flooding is ongoing or\nexpected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding in and around the Moenkopi Wash.\n\nSOURCE...River gauge reported.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of areas in and around the\nMoenkopi Wash.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nMoenkopi.\n\nThis includes the following highways...\nHighway 160 between mile markers 318 and 321. U.S. Highway 89 between\nmile markers 476 and 478. State Route 264 between mile markers 323\nand 324.\n\nThis includes the following creeks, washes and rivers...\nLittle Colorado River, Begashibito Wash, Fivemile Wash, Moenkopi\nWash and Hamblin Wash.",
                "instruction": "This is a life threatening situation. Heavy rainfall will cause\nextensive and severe flash flooding of creeks...streams...and ditches\nin the Moenkopi Wash. Severe debris flows can also be anticipated\nacross roads. Roads and driveways may be washed away in places. If\nyou encounter flood waters...climb to safety.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
